# .dockerignore for ../../Dockerfile's intended build context (the repo
# root — see that file's header comment for why). Plain ".dockerignore"
# files are only auto-applied by Docker/BuildKit when they sit at the
# *build context's* root, or (BuildKit only) when renamed to match the
# Dockerfile's context-relative path, e.g.
# "packages/muan-companion-server/Dockerfile.dockerignore". This file
# living here is for discoverability next to the Dockerfile it belongs to;
# to make it actually take effect when building with `-f
# packages/muan-companion-server/Dockerfile .` from the repo root, either
# copy/symlink it to the repo root as ".dockerignore", or duplicate it as
# "packages/muan-companion-server/Dockerfile.dockerignore" (same content,
# BuildKit-only auto-pickup). See muan-companion.md "Docker" for the
# verified build command and this caveat.

.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-ssr
.slidev
.vite-inspect
.nuxt
.output
*.local
.env
*.pdf
*-export
components.d.ts
docs/.vitepress/cache
cypress/downloads
cypress/videos
cypress/screenshots
.DS_Store
.eslintcache
.idea
